[{"id":14,"name":"AlphaRAR.IsCondExp","kind":"Structure","keyword":"structure","module":"AlphaRAR.Mathlib.CondExp","package":"AlphaRAR","isProp":false,"hashes":{"meaning":"33b314f29a008492","local":"dcfc49bff255b20f","content":"a4991e3e92baf34f"},"doc":"**`g` is a version of the conditional expectation of `f` given `m`.**\n\nThe measure and the sub-σ-algebra come first so that `Measure α` still elaborates against the\nambient `m0` rather than against `m`, and so that the characterized object `g` is the last\nargument. ","statement":{"binders":[{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"α","role":"type","type":"Type u_1","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"E","role":"type","type":"Type u_2","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"head":"NormedAddCommGroup","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"NormedAddCommGroup E","typeRefs":[[0,18,"NormedAddCommGroup"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"NormedSpace","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"NormedSpace ℝ E","typeRefs":[[0,11,"NormedSpace"],[12,13,"Real"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"m0","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace α","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":true,"head":"MeasureTheory.Measure","implicit":false,"name":"μ","role":"variable","type":"MeasureTheory.Measure α","typeRefs":[[0,21,"MeasureTheory.Measure"]]},{"explicit":true,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":false,"name":"m","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace α","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":true,"implicit":false,"name":"f","role":"variable","type":"α → E","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":true,"implicit":false,"name":"g","role":"variable","type":"α → E","typeRefs":[]}],"conclusion":"Prop","conclusionRefs":[],"decl":"AlphaRAR.IsCondExp","fields":[{"name":"aestronglyMeasurable","type":"MeasureTheory.AEStronglyMeasurable g μ","typeRefs":[[0,34,"MeasureTheory.AEStronglyMeasurable"]]},{"name":"integrableOn","type":"∀ (s : Set α), MeasurableSet s → μ s < ⊤ → MeasureTheory.IntegrableOn g s μ","typeRefs":[[7,10,"Set"],[15,28,"MeasurableSet"],[37,38,"LT.lt"],[39,40,"Top.top"],[43,69,"MeasureTheory.IntegrableOn"]]},{"name":"setIntegral_eq","type":"∀ (s : Set α), MeasurableSet s → μ s < ⊤ → ∫ (x : α) in s, g x ∂μ = ∫ (x : α) in s, f x ∂μ","typeRefs":[[7,10,"Set"],[15,28,"MeasurableSet"],[37,38,"LT.lt"],[39,40,"Top.top"],[43,44,"MeasureTheory.integral"],[53,55,"MeasureTheory.integral"],[63,64,"MeasureTheory.integral"],[66,67,"Eq"],[68,69,"MeasureTheory.integral"],[78,80,"MeasureTheory.integral"],[88,89,"MeasureTheory.integral"]]}]},"code":"/-- **`g` is a version of the conditional expectation of `f` given `m`.**\n\nThe measure and the sub-σ-algebra come first so that `Measure α` still elaborates against the\nambient `m0` rather than against `m`, and so that the characterized object `g` is the last\nargument. -/\nstructure IsCondExp (μ : Measure α) (m : MeasurableSpace α) (f g : α → E) : Prop where\n  /-- `g` is measurable for the smaller σ-algebra: it uses only the information in `m`. -/\n  aestronglyMeasurable : AEStronglyMeasurable[m] g μ\n  /-- `g` is integrable on every `m`-measurable set of finite measure. -/\n  integrableOn : ∀ s, MeasurableSet[m] s → μ s < ∞ → IntegrableOn g s μ\n  /-- `g` averages `f` correctly: it has the same integral as `f` over every `m`-measurable set of\n  finite measure. This is the content; the other two fields are what make it pin `g` down. -/\n  setIntegral_eq : ∀ s, MeasurableSet[m] s → μ s < ∞ → ∫ x in s, g x ∂μ = ∫ x in s, f x ∂μ","proof":"","source":{"path":"AlphaRAR/Mathlib/CondExp.lean","start":37,"end":49,"url":"https://github.com/RemyDegenne/alpha-rar/blob/e7164a80baea3f4f65e108de31d2d561dd35e350/AlphaRAR/Mathlib/CondExp.lean#L37-L49"},"deps":[],"outside":[],"external":[["DFunLike.coe","mathlib","definition"],["ENNReal","mathlib","definition"],["ENNReal.instPartialOrder","mathlib","instance"],["ENNReal.instTop","mathlib","instance"],["Eq","lean4","inductive"],["LT.lt","l